    "explanation": "To the driver and the rider: the question is whether the 5.00 SGD no-show fee charged on TRP-05061 should stand, and I find that it should.\n\nTimeline from the platform's own records. Driver D-25029 accepted the trip at 17:45:30 and the trip record's arrival event (EV-TRIP-05061) puts him at the pickup at Singapore Expo Hall 2 at 17:53:40. The driver-device GPS trace (EV-GPS-05061) corroborates this: its nearest fix is 26.2 m from the recorded pickup coordinate at 17:53:00 with a reported accuracy of 5 m, inside the 120 m large-venue arrival radius POL-NS-21 sets, and the check returns corroborated = true. This was an on-demand trip (trip_record.scheduled_at is null), so the 300-second free wait ran from arrival, 17:53:40 to 17:58:40, and had already expired when the driver cancelled at 18:00:10 (390 s after arrival). POL-NS-21's precondition for cancelling as a rider no-show is met. Before cancelling, the driver sent two in-app messages (17:54:00 and 17:57:10, both delivered and read) and placed one in-app call (17:58:20, unanswered, ringing 35 s), so POL-NS-23's contact obligation is satisfied. The amount charged was exactly 5.00 SGD (EV-FARE-05061), which is the POL-NS-22 no-show fee, so that fee stands and is the driver's compensation for time and fuel.\n\nThe rider's account is answered, not ignored. The rider says the driver was not at the pickup point she set at the Hall 2 entrance and never called. The arrival test in POL-NS-21 measures against the trip record's pickup coordinate and radius, not a separately stated meeting point, and the trace corroborates it; the driver wrote to the rider at 17:54:00 that he was at the 'Hall 2 taxi and private hire pick-up bay, lane 3', both messages were read (17:54:41 and 17:57:58), and she was pushed 'Your driver has arrived' at 17:53:44. The trip record's own in_app_calls entry records the driver's 17:58:20 call, so 'he never called me' is not borne out. The rider's request that the case be escalated under POL-GEN-26 because the driver's position vis-a-vis the rider's chosen point cannot be established is declined: the fact the rules need - that the driver was at the pickup - is carried by two artifacts graded COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and POL-GEN-26 applies only where the evidence that would carry a needed fact is missing or impaired.\n\nMoney. The 5.00 SGD fee was charged on 31 Aug 2026 at 18:00:14, then refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver at 21:11:10 as an interim measure pending review (EV-FARE-05061, payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 5.00). Because the fee stands on the merits, that 5.00 SGD belongs to the driver, and since the driver filed, the outcome is read against the present state: DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00. These are the same 5.00 SGD figure, not two payments, and nothing is returned to the rider. No referral is produced: the fee is exactly the policy 5.00 SGD (so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not fire), the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not apply because the driver did not miss any arrival deadline, and rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is 0, below POL-NS-25's threshold of 3. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, neither party carries a fraud flag, and POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final; confidence is 0.95, against artifacts all at weight 1.0. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05061-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and nothing here rests on it."
